<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-AUSTRALIAN RATE CUTS STILL TO BE FELT-GOVT.</title>
<headline>RTRS-AUSTRALIAN RATE CUTS STILL TO BE FELT-GOVT.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian Employment minister Amanda Vanstone said on Thursday the effects of recent interest rate cuts were yet to be felt and that economic fundamentals for sustained growth were extremely positive.</p>
<p>Vanstone was commenting in a statement after data earlier showed Australian employment rose 21,300 in July and unemployment also rose to 8.7 percent in July from 8.5 percent in June.</p>
</text>
